66247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147621 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying True Statements Given Some Polyhedra Nets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147621 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147621 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "21ee2869-b51d-5bb3-82dc-7c8d48f229b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1045 "Nets of Polyhedrons" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186148631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147668 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "6e71d7e9-f2d0-55e1-9d6b-91487d023e2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147920 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147920 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the net of a triangular pyramid?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45f04d23-d77f-5812-a1db-56097793a5ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147920 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by portraying our triangular pyramid:\n\n![](images/05/0599b93689ea7066815bca05706eb44cf4fcea5eee12482ad3e2e7360a063b5c.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIf we were to unfold the pyramid above along its edges, we'd get the net shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/94/94e87252eb416f9424cb191e060a3e7294d130349c77a8fd87d2c12051378aa8.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/c6/c603092d3d64352abf3746123afd04c58be06c56d917c6e53123fab8ea4d1d17.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147930 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147930 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61894" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147930 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147930 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a1/a1cb5b4cb90a334dbbd2ae44d68317680db16ff269b57f51072c7d8e965bb476.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids depicted above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147930 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "049160b7-7b99-52f8-99eb-7ab178d7e1b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147930 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the nets of each solid.\n\n![](images/e9/e9168bf41b10db4e0d353aa09682a7fe048216a0ccf28fd196daaf5bf7fd3fff.png)\n\n \n\nAs we can see, the correct answer is:\n\n$\\,$ *\"The net of III consists of $1$ rectangle and $4$ triangles.\"*\n\nOther statements are false. \n\n- *\"The net of II consists of triangles only\"* is false since the net of II has $3$ rectangles (the side faces).\n\n- *\"The net of I has one triangle\"* is not true because the net of I contains only squares.\n\n- *\"The net of III consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles\"* is false since the net of III only has $1$ rectangle (the base of the solid).\n\n- *\"The net of I consists of exactly $8$ squares\"* is not true because the net of I only has $6$ squares." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148597 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148597 #edb/ref 1061 9273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148597 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "df23bcaa-b2b0-56df-a6ec-d3053fc905de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148597 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148600 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148600 #edb/ref 1061 9277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148600 #edb/ref 1062 