2186566247 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566247 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566247 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566247 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/56/5683cb4560a5715654c795d94f4123c79a758e281ef40b92cccb379482506c2c.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids depicted above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "776cd40d-1c79-55ee-9771-1ee0329ddc24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566247 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the nets of each solid.\n\n![](images/27/277d5aa8a8116d230bf000ef7d8e94a071acbf499a49b9d8b911a4e89cfaf18a.png)\n\n \n\nAs we can see, the correct answer is:\n\n$\\,$ *\"The net of II consists of triangles only\"*\n\nOther statements are false. \n\n- *\"The net of III consists of triangles only\"* is false since the net of III has one rectangle (the base of the solid).\n\n- *\"The net of I consists of $3$ triangles and $3$ rectangles\"* is not true because the net of I contains only $2$ triangles (the base and the top of the solid).\n\n- *\"The net of III consists of $3$ triangles and $1$ rectangle\"* is false since the net of III has $4$ triangles (the side faces).\n\n- *\"The net of II consists of $3$ triangles and $1$ rectangle\"* is not true because the net of II does not contain rectangles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566248 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566248 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566248 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566248 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f5/f5be9bb97784c25d555d4581bc67916ab0b8e57ade33619b3df27d2eb0f59db2.png)\n\nThe net of which polyhedron is shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f868203-0afb-5c74-9f79-f3b6b4ea5865" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566248 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/d9/d9010650127d8dcfcd387df09b9dce689ece90e3912ede882241c8b714f91d45.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIf we were to fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, we'd get a triangular pyramid.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/6b/6bf9ac2bd130fdad3a056d0e5680e010003366f115e3655de59bbd795d1513f5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566253 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566253 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566253 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566253 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is **not** the net of a prism?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566253 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95eb11a1-9c88-5c12-9e33-b81f6a14bd8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566253 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/e7/e7017b17e88561231e151d48fe5337bc82d164639f785eda0b0b148c9ee80b37.png)\n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a rectangular pyramid, as shown below:\n\n![](images/5e/5e32ef37ef2dae4c714afcb744820c8fb1cbbc3bd23f7347552b3a7bc73949bc.png)\n\nSo, the net that does not correspond to a prism is:\n\n![](images/c3/c35316b772366403fca0d0ba030866a82ef0d7c411c2817aa7e1feffa894c96e.png)\n\n   \n\nThe rest of the given nets will give us a (triangular or rectangular) prism." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566261 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566261 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566261 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566261 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/41/416f9df81e2159b58bddde964435f97fac3e461ce984402c2ea22616bc0edd48.png)\n\nThe net of which polyhedron is shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566261 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bcd25659-0e9d-5735-91bb-5b7182253798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566261 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/b2/b2ea30cd84f4d52f5d1e4a910817399c892c38a4b87ec7773eace67000a865fd.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIf we were to fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, we'd get a rectangular pyramid.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/a0/a097a94ed0fa5ed23cf4e9b2ae36319ee2a00fb276b8b0bd1fe21999c1887f0f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566275 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566275 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is **not** the net of a prism?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff018c25-43d3-5a1d-9dbc-90c62eb5eb4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566275 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/d9/d9010650127d8dcfcd387df09b9dce689ece90e3912ede882241c8b714f91d45.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIf we were to fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, we'd get a triangular pyramid.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/6b/6bf9ac2bd130fdad3a056d0e5680e010003366f115e3655de59bbd795d1513f5.png)\n\nSo, the net that does not correspond to a prism is:\n\n![](images/f5/f5be9bb97784c25d555d4581bc67916ab0b8e57ade33619b3df27d2eb0f59db2.png)\n\nThe rest of the given nets will give us a (triangular or rectangular) prism." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
